  "strategy": "# Approach and rationale\nThe current DE + SLSQP pipeline struggles with the nonconvex overlap objective and may converge to suboptimal local minima. We propose an improved strategy using convex relaxation and a differentiable surrogate objective to better navigate the challenging optimization landscape.\n\n# Mathematical specification\nWe define the step function h \u2208 [0,1]^n_points and seek to minimize:\nC\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222b h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx\n\nWe reformulate the problem by introducing a differentiable surrogate for the max operation:\nC\u2085_approx = (1/\u03c4) * log(\u03a3 exp(\u03c4 * c\u2096))\nwhere \u03c4 > 0 is a temperature parameter controlling the sharpness of the surrogate.\n\n# Implementation procedure\n1. Initialize n_points = 200 (for better resolution while keeping computation feasible)\n2. Read initial_h_values and interpolate to new resolution\n3. Normalize initial_h to satisfy sum(h) = n_points / 2 = 100\n4. Define the convex relaxation optimization problem:\n   Minimize \u03a3 (h_i (1 - h_{i + k}) * dx) for all k\n   Subject to:\n   0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n   \u03a3 h_i = 100\n5. Use a combination of convex optimization and gradient descent:\n   a. Preprocess the problem into a form suitable for CVXPY\n   b. Apply log-sum-exp relaxation\n   c. Use gradient descent with adaptive learning rate\n6. Validate and repair feasibility after each iteration\n\n# Search choices and useful variations\nDefault parameters:\n- \u03c4 = 0.1\n- CVXPY solver: MOSEK\n- Gradient descent steps: 200\n- Learning rate: 1e-3\nVariations:\n- Adjust \u03c4 for different surrogate sharpness\n- Try different solvers (ECOS, SCS)\n- Change n_points to trade-off resolution vs computation time\n\n# Compute budget and robustness\nTotal budget: <80s\n- Initial setup: 5s\n- Optimization: 70s\n- Validation: 5s\n\nRobustness checks:\n- Track improvement over iterations to detect stagnation\n- Maintain best solution found so far\n- Handle infeasible intermediate solutions by projection\n\n# Validation and return contract\nEnsure:\n- 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n- \u03a3 h_i = 100\n- Evaluate with original C\u2085 objective\n- Compute max overlap at all lags",
